{"h":3209,"lines":[{"h":0.017417409783954563,"c":1,"x":0.82278847996506144,"w":0.080807183583577413,"t":"Reading","y":0.038203197496247787},{"x":0.071735142522584089,"y":0.08531188561859393,"w":0.7633131408691407,"c":1,"h":0.022431836469893884,"t":"His plans for a modern and 'rational' city were consistent with Renaissance ideals. But, in"},{"y":0.10693855413953401,"x":0.069835570986325216,"w":0.75545989990234375,"t":"keeping with his personality, Leonardo included several innovations in his urban design.","h":0.020235966002086991,"c":1},{"x":0.069853133889673041,"w":0.79815572102864574,"t":"Leonardo wanted the city to be built on several levels, linked with vertical outdoor staircases.","y":0.12628622583227322,"h":0.020205246399496168,"c":1},{"y":0.14339359791156758,"t":"This design can be seen in some of today's high-rise buildings but was unconventional at the","c":1,"h":0.021150288329317535,"w":0.79043894449869789,"x":0.069828453701296103},{"h":0.023004601974724981,"c":1,"w":0.83517852783203128,"y":0.16217953596707102,"t":"time. Indeed, this idea of taking full advantage of the interior spaces wasn't implemented until the","x":0.06978928878152639},{"x":0.058168905787085286,"w":0.53030517578124992,"y":0.18181088569282222,"c":1,"h":0.022990346177716114,"t":"1920s and 1930s, with the birth of the Modernist movement."},{"t":"While in the upper layers of the city, people could walk undisturbed between elegant palaces","y":0.2208722743880962,"w":0.78834950764973954,"x":0.07184466360474194,"h":0.019003115264797477,"c":1},{"x":0.069795279867411936,"y":0.23770349936317581,"t":"and streets, the lower layer was the place for services, trade, transport and industry. But the","w":0.77691624959309891,"c":1,"h":0.021926777682200416},{"h":0.020629559573354772,"t":"true originality of Leonardo's vision was its fusion of architecture and engineering. Leonardo","w":0.79429631551106772,"c":1,"x":0.069839718858088609,"y":0.25585836479183599},{"t":"designed extensive hydraulic plants to create artificial canals throughout the city. The canals,","h":0.017488046450035655,"c":1,"x":0.069902906353387764,"y":0.27757009319312986,"w":0.79223302205403645},{"h":0.020731781576281416,"x":0.069816326435033979,"t":"regulated by clocks and basins, were supposed to make it easier for boats to navigate inland.","w":0.78849624633789062,"c":1,"y":0.2941399681177278},{"c":1,"x":0.071780715610115828,"y":0.3133306309606011,"w":0.77682622273763025,"t":"Leonardo also thought that the width of the streets ought to match the average height of the","h":0.01999731331228094},{"h":0.017580417383497027,"x":0.069902905637741805,"y":0.33271028039792339,"w":0.82330098470052082,"t":"adjacent houses: a rule still followed in many contemporary cities across Italy, to allow access to","c":1},{"w":0.45436894734700517,"y":0.3531976745111477,"h":0.015988371899566256,"x":0.069902904878827984,"c":1,"t":"sun and reduce the risk of damage from earthquakes."},{"c":1,"x":0.071776146345481684,"t":"Although some of these features existed in Roman cities, before Leonardo's drawings there had","w":0.81374989827473954,"h":0.020925394694010446,"y":0.38752239459254922},{"c":1,"t":"never been a multi-level, compact modern city which was thoroughly technically conceived.","x":0.071742246786959826,"h":0.021786665396526961,"w":0.78852101643880212,"y":0.4053399038719292},{"t":"Indeed, it wasn't until the 19th century that some of his ideas were applied. For example, the","w":0.79232650756835932,"c":1,"h":0.019232022056698495,"y":0.42581895731860064,"x":0.069862537961514398},{"h":0.018895348284474922,"w":0.8194174702962238,"t":"subdivision of the city by function - with services and infrastructures located in the lower levels","x":0.071844662837032447,"y":0.44476744213398667,"c":1},{"h":0.021338171082493584,"c":1,"w":0.81377985636393235,"t":"and wide and well-ventilated boulevards and walkways above for residents - is an idea that can","x":0.071745463815841695,"y":0.46173743321827088},{"x":0.07184464953298933,"y":0.48099688444833788,"t":"be found in Georges-Eugène Haussmann's renovation of Paris under Emperor Napoleon III","h":0.019003115264797366,"w":0.77864079793294272,"c":1},{"x":0.071844662995431935,"w":0.21165047963460284,"h":0.016199376947040545,"c":1,"t":"between 1853 and 1870.","y":0.50280373817188662},{"h":0.020698334643402538,"w":0.7845830281575521,"y":0.53614248017768662,"t":"Today, Leonardo's ideas are not simply valid, they actually suggest a way forward for urban","x":0.071786058742824441,"c":1},{"w":0.74964686075846354,"t":"planning. Many scholars think that the compact city, built upwards instead of outwards,","c":1,"x":0.071758762406485821,"y":0.55473744040806272,"h":0.022087457246869557},{"c":1,"x":0.069902920688145687,"y":0.57412790723857654,"w":0.80194173177083328,"h":0.019018510123279597,"t":"integrated with nature (especially water systems), with efficient transport infrastructure, could"},{"t":"help modern cities become more efficient and sustainable. This is yet another reason why","x":0.071794351522012981,"h":0.019865571375576541,"y":0.59213156791457955,"w":0.76125747680664069,"c":1},{"w":0.80207341512044283,"t":"Leonardo was aligned so closely with modern urban planning and centuries ahead of his time.","y":0.61089546398802952,"h":0.021463079244548267,"x":0.071776032557703401,"c":1},{"x":0.87961165128338359,"t":"49","c":1,"w":0.029126211802164681,"y":0.9534883721282581,"h":0.015988371899566145}],"w":2400}